        <definition>NDXLChannel * ndxlGetNetworkFirstChannel</definition>
        <argsstring>(NDXLNetwork *_Network)</argsstring>
        <name>ndxlGetNetworkFirstChannel</name>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="group__ndxl__objects_1gaefd105209efdd9f61bea4c3f76770d37" kindref="member">NDXLNetwork</ref> *</type>
          <declname>_Network</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Gets the first noise channel in a network. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">_Network</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Target network to retrieve the first noise channel of.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>If _Network is either NULL or has no noise channels, returns NULL, otherwise returns the first <ref refid="ndxlcore_8h_1a40b73c1a687ab1376515b42d4294c079" kindref="member">NDXLChannel</ref> pointer created on _Network.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>This function is most commonly used in conjunction with ndxlGetNetworkNextChannel, ndxlGetNetworkPreviousChannel, and/or ndxlGetNetworkLastChannel to iterate over network noise channels.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>A return value of NULL does not necessarily indicate an error, as the network could have no channels. If unsure, use <ref refid="group__ndxl__err_1ga431ccb893f54f2ce7fe5ead2a8abd3cf" kindref="member">ndxlGetLastErrorCode()</ref> to check.</para>
</simplesect>
